Robert Jarratt wrote:
> 
> The external device is a TK50Z, it is fitted with a terminator, it works 
> fine on a 3100 M38 using a BC56H cable. The two cables I have used are 
> about 60cm and 150cm respectively. I am suspicious of the quality of the 
> connection, it is always a fight to get the clips to hold the connector 
> on. I have reseated the internal connection so I will try that again.

Is it a TK50Z-FA or TK50Z-GA?  The -FA was for the MV2000 and pretty 
much assumes that it is the only thing on the bus.

The -GA was for the 3100 and is much more accepting of other devices on 
the bus.

The differences between the -FA and -GA are (1) ROMs and (2) the -GA has 
external SCSI ID switches.  You can put the -GA ROMs into a -FA.

Sometimes, some combinations of SCSI devices just don't work.

