Related to my Jan 25th 09 post re KFQSA DSSI in BA23 or BA11.

Related to my Nov 12th 08 post re DSSI -> BA353 possible?

I posted asking whether the BA353 could host an HSD05.   Alfred Falk
and Kari Uusim=E4ki were kind enough to provide tips.   I succeeded in
getting the configuration working so am posting the process here.


My test system is a Vaxstation III in a BA11: KA650 CPU, MS650 16mb
RAM, VCB01 video controller, KFQSA DSSI controller with an external
BA353 hosting an HSD05 and 2 RZ26 drives.


To get SCSI drives working with a KA650/KFQSA via HSD05 in a BA353:

Process requires a CPU monitor with advanced console commands like
CONFIGURE
 and SET HOST/DUP/UQSSP/DISK 0 thus cannot be done with eg. KA630.

Cabling:

T&S50 =3D tab and socket 50 (eg. host adapter)
MR50 =3D microribbon 50 (eg. trilink connector on HSD05)

- used Berg50 female -> Berg50 male cable as an extender from KFQSA.
- used Berg50 female -> T&S50 cable as the bus cable.
- used T&S50 -> MR50 (BC29R-06) cable as device cable to HSD05 port 1.
- attached DSSI MR50 type terminator to HSD05 port 2.
- on SCSI bus, HSD05 terminates one end (slot 1), and a SCSI2
terminator
   terminates other end (upper port on rear).

HSD05:
- set DSSI ID =3D 0.
- set SCSI ID =3D 6. (using 7 for PC connection on rear).
- set termination active, SCSI term power on, DSSI term power off.
   DSSI term power provided by KFQSA.

