If you have checked everything else (cables, connectors, termination, 
termination power, cable [bus] length), there is one more thing that 
might affect the SCSI bus is the different "generations" (SCSI-1, 
SCSI-2, SCSI-3) of SCSI devices. The adapter inside the MicroVAX 3100-80 
is SCSI-1 or "slow" SCSI and it does not know of the newer SCSI 
generations. Therefore it is always capable only of 5MB/s speeds. The 
newer devices are capable of working with older adapters BUT it is not 
always flawless. That's why it might be that the new device you are 
trying to use with the MicroVAX doesn't succeed to negotiate the right 
speed with the adapter (initiator).


Regards,

Kari


